  "method": {
    "allocations": "Separate tracemalloc runs record global traced peak and allocation differences still retained at the end. They do not count every temporary allocation or give an uninstrumented runtime.",
    "cache": "The existing encoder's text-byte cache is limited to 16777216 bytes per evaluator. Its dictionary keys and object overhead are additional; the existing process address-space limit still applies.",
    "causality": "For each size, mutate a later invented bar and compare the earlier complete strategy state after temporary in-memory projection of the dataset identifier, which hashes the full input.",
    "indicators": "Through-index, mapping size and clock bound are recorded for every call. Prefix totals show overlapping work; a repeated selector is only a matching recorded selector, not a proof of identical data. The evidence retains 100-bar prefix-length bins and aggregate CPU; the profiler prints all individual selectors.",
    "integers": "Each return from the frozen integer converter is counted. Distinct values use exact integer equality. Character totals count returned decimal characters, including signs, across the reference evaluation.",
    "profile": "Isolated V2 reference evaluations under cProfile and counters. Self and cumulative CPU are separately recorded. Instrumentation overhead is substantial and cumulative functions overlap.",
    "prototype": "Four alternating runs of each candidate measured only the reference evaluator. The selection was confirmed by separate complete worker measurements.",
    "rejection_views": "Separately reconstruct the exact RejectionBarV2 dictionaries for each prefix and finalization; input dictionary construction is outside the measurement.",
    "reproducibility": "Run the three parametrizations of test_alternating_complete_workers for four alternating pairs per size. Run the bounded profile tool with 201, 401 or 601 and optionally --allocation.",
    "scope": "Invented dense prefixes of 201, 401 and 601 observations; no registered 1000 or 5000 replay.",
    "worker_comparison": "Four alternating V2/V3 process pairs per size under the original supervisor, CPU, wall, memory, file and physical limits. CPU includes startup, fixture generation, test bootstrap, registration checks, both engines, byte comparison and receipt output. Small test-only fixtures are substituted at the contract boundary and do not constitute a production-tier receipt."
  },
